Sure! To pull the statistics for gigabit‑Ethernet interfaces on the `test-fab` fabric, I’ll need the base URL (or IP address) of the telemetry API endpoint. Once I have that, I can make a GET request like this:

```python
response = requests_get({
    "url": "https://<API_IP>/sedgeapi/v1/cisco-nir/api/api/telemetry/flowrules/interfaceInfo",
    "params": {
        "fabricName": "test-fab",
        "interfaceType": "gigabitethernet",
        "infoType": "statistics"
    }
})
```

Could you please provide the API’s IP address or full base URL so I can fetch the data for you?
